>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `register_quotient`

``` hol4
Refute.register_quotient :
  {qty : hol_type,
   rty : hol_type,
   abs : term,
   rep : term,
   equiv_thm : thm} -> unit
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Registers an existing quotient type with the model finder.

`qty` is the quotient type and `rty` its representation type; `abs` and
`rep` must be existing constants of types `rty -> qty` and `qty -> rty`.
`equiv_thm` must be hypothesis-free and either a bare
`QUOTIENT equiv abs rep` theorem or a total equivalence
`!x y. R x y <=> (R x = R y)`.  Only the `QUOTIENT` shape names the
Abs/Rep constants, so only it is cross-checked against `abs` and `rep`.
The shape selects the encoding: a `QUOTIENT` bridge uses the sound
partial encoding, and a total equivalence drops that encoding's then
redundant domain axiom.

Registrations are session-local; a valid later registration replaces
the same quotient operator.  The model finder also harvests standard
quotient metadata lazily; explicit registration serves a nonstandard
database location or shape.

### Failure

Fails for malformed parameter types, nonconstant or ill-typed Abs/Rep
terms, free or ill-typed equivalence relations, an unsupported theorem
shape, theorem hypotheses, a theorem naming different constants, or an
incompatible datatype, codatatype, typedef, or fraction classification.

### See also

[`Refute.register_typedef`](#Refute.register_typedef),
[`Refute.register_codatatype`](#Refute.register_codatatype),
[`Refute.register_frac_type`](#Refute.register_frac_type),
[`Refute.harvest_registrations`](#Refute.harvest_registrations),
[`Refute.model_refute`](#Refute.model_refute)

Quotient encoding is described in \ref{Description:the-holrefute-library}.
